{"name":"Cherished One","hex":"#fc9293","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cherished","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["highly valued, having a high personal value."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of cherish"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherished"},{"term":"one","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["NATO & ICAO radiotelephony clear code (spelling-alphabet name) for the digit 1."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Oneida."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/one"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cherished","blocks":[{"text":"Cherished is the fourteenth studio album by American singer-actress Cher, released on June 4, 1977, as Cher's final studio album released by Warner Bros. Records. This album, like several other predecessors, was a commercial failure and failed to chart. The album was promoted by the release of the lead single, \"Pirate\" which charted at No. 93 on the Billboard Hot 100 and a second single, \"War Paint and Soft Feathers\" which failed to chart. \"Pirate\" was the only single from the 70s Warner era to chart despite the album being her lowest selling album of her entire career."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e2/Cherished.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherished","wikidata":"Q965141"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e2/Cherished.jpg/250px-Cherished.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e2/Cherished.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e2/Cherished.jpg/250px-Cherished.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org